--- SURFACE NOTES: AutomationCard (parity port of web/src/features/automations/pages/AutomationCard.tsx) ---
Files (allowed scope + the standard headless test wiring the sibling surfaces also use):
  - feature-views/AutomationCard/AutomationCard.cs        (WinUI 3 view, sealed ContentControl, code-built)
  - feature-views/AutomationCard/AutomationCard.Model.cs  (WinUI-free model / projection / diagnostics /
                                                           registration; compiled into BOTH the app and the
                                                           headless test project)
  - TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/AutomationCardTests.cs (60 headless cases)
  - TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj          (one <Compile> link for AutomationCard.Model.cs)

Pure presentational card — the web component never fetches (its only data source is useTranslation; the page
passes the `automation` prop and callbacks). There is therefore no fetch-driven loading/empty/error/stale/
offline branch to reproduce — same precedent as the AlertCard / BatteryPill / AddWidgetButton leaves. EVERY
real conditional branch in the web source IS reproduced and unit-tested:
  * status: active (success badge) / disabled (neutral) / auto-disabled (danger) via getUIStatus precedence
    (auto_disabled > !enabled > active).
  * enable toggle state = auto_disabled ? false : enabled; the view re-routes an auto-disabled "turn on" to
    ReEnableRequested vs ToggleRequested (web handleToggle), and the re-enable item shows in the kebab menu.
  * isFiring -> cyan accent border (web ring-neon-cyan) + "Firing" chip; auto-disabled -> danger border.
  * description shown only when present (truncated).
  * scoped vehicle (Car glyph + name) vs "All vehicles".
  * last_triggered_at -> "Last: {ago}" (CheckCircle) vs "Never run" (SkipForward); "Runs: {n}";
    failure_count>0 -> "Fails: {n}" (XCircle); next_fire_time -> "Next: {formatDateTime}".
  * auto_disabled && reason -> danger reason banner.
  * conflicts[] -> one warning(amber)/info(blue) banner each, '"name" — reason'.
  * PinButton -> native pin/unpin affordance (IsPinned + PinToggleRequested), Pin/Unpin glyph + a11y name.
  * delete -> destructive TsConfirmDialog (title/message-with-name/Delete/Cancel) -> DeleteRequested.
Shared components: TsGlassPanel, TsBadge, TsToggle, TsButton, TsConfirmDialog, MenuFlyout, DisplayTokens,
StatusResources, DateTimeFormatting. No web Tailwind classes ported; platform tokens only.
Relative time is a 1:1 port of the card's bespoke timeAgo (— / "just now" / Xm / Xh / Xd ago).
i18n (ALL via the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade; no English literals in native code):
  translation.automations.status.{active,disabled,auto-disabled}, .firing, .toggleLabel, .menu, .testRun,
  .reEnable, .duplicate, .export, .delete, .allVehicles, .lastRun, .neverRun, .runs, .fails, .nextFire,
  .conflictWith, .deleteTitle, .deleteMessage ({0} name interpolation), .deleteConfirm; translation.common.cancel;
  translation.pin.pin, translation.pin.unpin. Keys absent from the resw catalog resolve via the facade English
  fallback (exactly as the web i18next returns a key's defaultValue) — verified by the ReswLocalizer test.
Accessibility: one composed Narrator name on the surface (name, status, vehicle, last/never run, runs, fails,
next fire, auto-disabled reason, conflicts); every interactive element named (pin -> Pin/Unpin; toggle ->
'Toggle automation'; kebab -> 'Actions menu'; each menu item by its label); decorative glyphs set
AccessibilityView.Raw; a WrapRow flow panel keeps the meta rows from clipping (web flex-wrap); no animation
(reduced-motion friendly).
Telemetry (P1/S11): view.opened slug=AutomationCard, PII-safe (never an automation name/description/vehicle/
conflict), emitted once on Loaded.

